  "speaker_notes": "Every morning a reviewer gets a ranked list of denials, each with a drafted letter, its evidence and a deadline. Nothing goes out without approval. That is an illustrative $2M to $4M a year, about 50 cents per appeal on the prototype. Show: three sources, one governed Databricks platform on AWS, a human gate before submission. For the architect: Lakeflow lands claims and notes in Unity Catalog, ai_query drafts each determination, and Lakebase serves the worklist.",
